WEBVTT

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.510
I suddenly had a craving 
for their cream puff.

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:22.270
I like the strawberry shortcake, but...

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:24.870
I can't forget the chocolate 
cake I had at the Seikyu Hotel.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:25.530
How was it?

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:29.740
It had a caramel mousse around it 
with a slight aroma of ginger...

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.780
They sent a new enemy to get 
the Prism Stones from us.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:42.720
It's hard on an ordinary middle school 
student who has a lot of things to do.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.270
That's...

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.660
Fujimura-kun...!

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:54.180
You'll get fat.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:54.630
No, I won't.

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.930
I'm going on a diet from next month.

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:03.200
Yukishiro-san said they were 
just childhood friends, but...

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.520
Did you know...?

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.290
Did you know, Nagisa?

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.360
Nagisa!

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.340
Were you listening to what I said?

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.990
Sorry, I wasn't listening.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.960
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.760
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.600
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:30.870
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.840
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.710
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.610
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:42.510
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.120
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.920
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot, we both</i>

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:52.020
<i>become stronger</i>

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:55.790
<i>and closer</i>

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:59.800
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:02.370
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.540
<i>Don't you know that good fortune 
comes to the gates of laughter?</i>

00:02:05.540 --> 00:02:08.410
<i>Out with the negative!</i>

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:14.680
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:15.580
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:18.280
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.090
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.990
<i>We're pretty and cure cure</i>

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.560
<i>Together we are</i>

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.630
<i>Pretty Cure...!</i>

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:37.990
"In spring, the dawn... 
The sky, dyed in morning

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:43.650
"light, slowly brightens and purple clouds

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:47.310
"stretch across the mountains... 
In summer, the night...

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.440
Once I start thinking about 
it, it really bothers me.

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.440
"I need not write of the 
nights lit by the moon..."

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:52.280
If they're childhood friends,

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.810
it means they've lived near each 
other since they were little,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.840
and their parents are good friends, too.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.890
Yukishiro-san's smart and elegant...

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:04.100
She's the complete opposite from me.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.890
If I were a boy, she'd 
be the type I'd fall for.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:09.110
Misumi-san?

00:03:09.110 --> 00:03:09.890
What?

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:11.200
Misumi-san!

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.130
Yes?

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:17.400
Would you care to continue 
reading from the textbook?

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:19.880
I'd be happy to.

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:24.070
Lately, don't you think that 
Nagisa hasn't been herself?

00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.900
No, she hasn't.

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:30.320
Yukishiro-san...?

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:35.750
What is it?

00:03:37.640 --> 00:03:39.080
W-Well...

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.030
Mipple! Mipple! Mipple!

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.510
That sounds like Mepple mipo!

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.140
Be quiet!

00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:47.840
Mipple!

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:50.320
Mepple!

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:59.280
You can't let people see you! 
Hurry, and go back inside!

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:00.410
Nagisa!

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.080
You should know how it 
feels to be in love mepo!

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.110
Why? Why is that mipo?

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:09.140
Actually, mepo...

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.790
What are you talking about?

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.710
Never mind that, Misumi-san...

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.100
Didn't you have something to say to me?

00:04:24.490 --> 00:04:26.920
Never mind... It wasn't anything important.

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:29.660
I was just getting to 
the important part mepo!

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:30.880
We're leaving.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:34.400
Mipple! I love you mepo!

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:42.390
"THE END OF PRETTY CURE! 
ISN'T IT TOO SOON FOR THAT?!"

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.070
That smells delectable mipo.

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.910
I wonder if Mepple is eating now, too mipo.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.370
You two are really close, aren't you?

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.650
I've waited for Mepple all this time 
here in the Field of Rainbows mipo.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:02.090
My heart will always belong to Mepple mipo.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.790
Don't you have anyone you love, Honoka mipo?

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:09.080
Someone I love?

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:12.020
Not really.

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:14.990
Then you must be lonely mipo.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:17.060
No...

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:20.430
I enjoy studying, and my 
extracurricular activities.

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:23.880
But it seems Nagisa is different mipo.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:30.260
It looks like she's interested 
in that guy, Fuji-P mipo.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.080
Fuji-P?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.250
Honoka?

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:34.370
Yes?

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:38.310
What is it, Grandmother?

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.340
I brought you tea.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.560
Thank you.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:43.430
Doing your homework?

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.320
Do you best.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:51.400
Come to think of it...

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:56.320
How is that friend of yours?

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:57.660
Friend?

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:01.110
You know, the cheerful and energetic 
girl who came here before.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.910
You mean Misumi-san?

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.070
That's right.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:08.540
You seemed to really be enjoying 
yourself when she was here.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:12.000
I was enjoying myself?

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:15.330
Yes, you were really enjoying yourself.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:20.620
Aren't you glad you found 
such a good friend, Honoka?

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:24.770
A friend...?

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.960
It's nothing to be concerned about...

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:33.700
But it bothers me.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:39.540
Sis! Lend me a CD...

00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:41.540
What are you doing?

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:45.010
I told you to knock before you come in!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:50.190
It's no wonder you don't have a boyfriend.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.740
It's none of your business!

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:59.350
Mom! Nagisa's picking on me!

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:04.760
I'm so sleepy.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.780
Misumi-san!

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.720
Childhood friends...?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.780
Good morning.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.170
Oh, good morning.

00:07:16.170 --> 00:07:17.180
It's green.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:22.520
Honoka...

00:07:23.110 --> 00:07:26.140
This week's after school 
student body meetings...

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:28.890
It's on Tuesday and Thursday...

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:32.810
Can't we cut it down to once a week?

00:07:32.810 --> 00:07:35.730
This is an important time 
for our soccer team, too.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:38.170
After all, I'm the team captain...

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:41.270
I feel bad about leaving it all to Kimata.

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.850
You've always been like that 
haven't you, Fujimura-kun?

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:51.070
Always...?

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:52.860
When you start thinking about soccer,

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:54.820
you can't see anything else.

00:07:55.380 --> 00:07:57.850
I know... I'm just a soccer nut.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:11.450
What's wrong?

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:13.170
Come to think of it...

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:16.780
I've never introduced 
the two of you properly.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:22.860
This is Nagisa Misumi... 
We're in the same class.

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:23.810
H-Hello.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:25.210
This is...

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:27.350
I'm Shogo Fujimura, third 
year, Boys Division.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:28.280
Nice to meet you.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.400
Everyone calls him Fuji-P.

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.370
Fuji-P?

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:38.010
I told you not to call me Fuji-P, didn't I?

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.370
We're not in grade school anymore.

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:41.900
Hey, Fuji-P!

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:43.620
You, too, Kimata!

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.510
What are you so upset about 
so early in the morning?

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:48.500
You must have a calcium deficiency.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:52.000
Eat more "niboshi" (dried baby 
sardines), right, Honoka?

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:55.770
They seem really close.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:59.450
But I'm glad I could introduce 
you to Fujimura-kun, Misumi-san.

00:09:00.610 --> 00:09:03.960
You wanted to talk to him, didn't you?

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:06.280
Yukishiro-san!

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:09.180
What's going on?

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:10.090
I have no idea.

00:09:10.090 --> 00:09:11.500
How could you...

00:09:12.090 --> 00:09:13.630
How could you!

00:09:14.340 --> 00:09:15.870
I don't believe this!

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:17.530
Misumi-san!

00:09:20.250 --> 00:09:22.600
Did I say something wrong?

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:29.650
Wait, Misumi-san!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:30.750
Did I do something?

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:32.350
That was uncalled for!

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:38.760
I thought it would be nice if I gave you 
the chance to talk to Fujimura-kun...

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:40.800
I never asked you to do that!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.780
You have no right!

00:09:43.510 --> 00:09:46.620
How would you know what I want?

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:50.880
Or do you always think that you're right?

00:09:51.310 --> 00:09:53.040
Aren't you being insensitive?

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:55.930
Insensitive...?

00:09:55.930 --> 00:09:59.610
How would you know how I feel?

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:01.030
Misumi-san...?

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.810
Just leave me alone!

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:06.760
The two of us may be Pretty Cure,

00:10:06.760 --> 00:10:08.890
but other than that, we're 
not friends or anything!

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.020
You're right...

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:30.810
I shouldn't have interfered.

00:11:03.080 --> 00:11:05.240
The two of us may be Pretty Cure,

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.210
but other than that, we're 
not friends or anything!

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:17.940
It feels good to eat outside 
once in a while, doesn't it?

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:21.420
It's great, isn't it, Nagisa?

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.870
Nagisa!

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:28.220
Did something happen?

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:32.940
Tell me! Come on! Tell me! Tell me!

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.310
Yukishiro-san?

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:43.880
What was that?

00:11:44.630 --> 00:11:47.050
Did you have a fight with Yukishiro-san?

00:11:48.630 --> 00:11:49.980
Sort of...

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:58.000
Why did I say that anyway?

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:07.410
Misumi

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:07.130
Nagisa!

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.990
If there's anything...

00:12:10.990 --> 00:12:12.170
Misumi-san?

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:16.190
Let's go, Shiho.

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:17.780
Wait, Rina!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:25.140
Nagisa... if you have a 
problem, just tell us.

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:28.990
No matter what happens, we're 
always on your side, Nagisa.

00:12:28.990 --> 00:12:32.410
That's right. We're friends, aren't we?

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.890
Thanks.

00:12:34.890 --> 00:12:36.220
We'll see you later.

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:41.860
I'm sorry about this morning.

00:12:42.350 --> 00:12:44.530
I've thought about it since then...

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:49.280
I have no right to have this...

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:55.760
At this rate, I may get you all upset again.

00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.870
And besides, with something like this,

00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:03.200
it's best to have two people 
who trust each other.

00:13:04.540 --> 00:13:05.450
So...

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.140
Yukishiro-san!

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:20.480
Is that happened while we were asleep mepo?

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:25.250
You need to make up with Honoka mipo!

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:27.170
I know.

00:13:27.720 --> 00:13:30.870
Then go over there now, 
and apologize to her mepo!

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:33.610
What are you doing mepo?

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:35.170
I thought I'd do my homework first.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.060
Are you trying to escape from reality mepo?

00:13:37.060 --> 00:13:39.060
I know, but...

00:13:39.550 --> 00:13:42.170
I don't know what to do.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.090
Then why don't you write down 
your feelings in that diary,

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:47.730
and try to sort them out mipo?

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:50.440
In this diary...?

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:53.270
You need the power of the 
Field of Light to read it,

00:13:53.270 --> 00:13:55.910
so no one else can read 
it, so don't worry mipo.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.670
My real feelings?

00:14:02.030 --> 00:14:12.120
No way! No way! No way! No way! No way!

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.320
Nagisa's gone over the edge mepo.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:12.120
Nagisa!

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:19.470
I know...

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:27.450
I have to give this diary back to Mipple.

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:37.090
Yukishiro-san! Good morning.

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:41.180
Good morning.

00:14:42.640 --> 00:14:44.620
Yukishiro-san...?

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:46.620
How about having lunch together?

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:52.070
I'm sorry.. I have a meeting about 
the student body from now...

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:55.650
Yukishiro-san!

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:59.120
That looks heavy. Shall I 
help you throw out the trash?

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.500
No... I can do it by myself.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.910
I pray that I can make up 
with Yukishiro-san tomorrow.

00:15:13.910 --> 00:15:16.210
Praying to the gods mepo?

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:18.990
You'd be praying, too, 
if you were in my shoes!

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:21.790
But with only five yen?

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:23.920
Get off my back!

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:25.850
I don't have much spending money this month!

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:38.530
Misumi-san?

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.780
Mipple! Mepple!

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.330
Misumi-san!

00:15:46.330 --> 00:15:49.130
Yukishiro-san? Behind you!

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:54.240
Yukishiro-san!

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:57.500
Uga!

00:16:00.290 --> 00:16:01.020
Uga!

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:02.660
Honoka!

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:03.970
You came mepo!

00:16:04.290 --> 00:16:05.780
Mipple! Mepple!

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.070
Hurry!

00:16:11.690 --> 00:16:13.340
Hurry and pass Mepple to me!

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.540
What are you doing? Hurry! Hurry!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:17.640
But I...

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.930
Get a move on!

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:24.200
I'm moving as fast as I can!

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:35.450
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:17:04.770 --> 00:17:07.270
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:10.130
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:13.880
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:17.380
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.810
Go back to where you came from!

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:25.440
For your information, I was 
moving as fast as I could!

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.660
That was just a figure of speech!

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.120
Don't nitpick!

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:33.290
And besides, I don't think 
that I am always right!

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:35.110
This isn't the time to be 
discussing that, is it?

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.750
But we have to talk it over!

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:41.570
It's just like a model student to think that 
we can resolve things by talking it over.

00:17:42.150 --> 00:17:44.010
Don't ignore me!

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:48.870
Talking things over is important 
in order to get to know each other.

00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.420
We're complete opposites, after all.

00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:53.850
You're right. We're entirely different.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:55.560
We're entirely different.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:57.050
We're too different!

00:17:57.410 --> 00:17:58.750
Enough to make me angry!

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:01.930
Don't interrupt!

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.300
We're having an important discussion here!

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:09.580
Black Thunder!

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:11.330
White Thunder!

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:20.950
The beautiful souls of Pretty Cure...!

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:23.910
...will crush the sinister hearts!

00:18:24.910 --> 00:18:28.150
Pretty Cure Marble Screw!

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:37.480
He turned into stars...

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:39.180
What awesome power!

00:18:39.670 --> 00:18:41.320
Thank goodness...

00:18:47.170 --> 00:18:49.150
That's how it is...

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:50.270
Goodbye.

00:18:52.870 --> 00:18:54.690
Is something wrong?

00:18:55.720 --> 00:18:58.020
We had a little fight...

00:18:58.570 --> 00:19:00.750
Maybe we don't get along, after all.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:03.130
What do you want to do, Honoka?

00:19:04.840 --> 00:19:08.700
What's important is what 
you want to do, isn't it?

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:11.810
Whether you get along or not is secondary.

00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:16.260
Especially if you care 
about the other person.

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:22.910
You know everything, don't you, Grandmother?

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:29.660
Of course! You're my precious granddaughter.

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:35.350
Why did it turn out like this?

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:37.390
What's wrong?

00:19:37.590 --> 00:19:41.590
I wanted to make up with her, 
but I lost my temper again.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:44.850
I'm such a lowlife.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:47.890
Fighting isn't a bad thing, is it?

00:19:49.180 --> 00:19:52.890
You wouldn't fight if you 
didn't care, would you?

00:19:59.100 --> 00:20:00.440
Be quiet!

00:20:02.980 --> 00:20:05.640
This diary is Misumi-san's...

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:19.700
Chocolate cake?

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:22.000
I love chocolate cake.

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:24.460
I've always hated onions.

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:29.470
"Misumi-san and I are entirely different."

00:20:30.890 --> 00:20:35.160
Our personalities, our way of thinking, 
and our values are different, too.

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:38.030
I don't know what she's thinking.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:41.260
I like being active.

00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:43.160
Studying is boring.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.450
I love the smell of grass.

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:49.390
My socks are a little smelly.

00:20:49.390 --> 00:20:51.740
Is it all like this?

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:55.740
I thought I was doing something good,

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:58.640
but I made her angry instead.

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:01.280
She sure uses a lot of Chinese characters.

00:21:02.940 --> 00:21:04.590
I love sunny days.

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:06.910
Rainy days are melancholy.

00:21:08.230 --> 00:21:09.930
I love my friends.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:13.290
I... don't like to fight.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:19.980
She and I are totally different, but...

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:22.630
I enjoy it when we're together.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:26.880
I want to get to know Yukishiro-san better.

00:21:27.920 --> 00:21:31.200
I want to be friends with Misumi-san.

00:21:37.210 --> 00:21:41.580
There's no way we can 
go on like this forever.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:45.610
Good morning!

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:48.550
Yukishiro-san? How did you know I was here?

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:49.850
I had a feeling...

00:21:53.570 --> 00:21:56.020
This is yours, Nagisa.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:00.520
It's your diary, isn't it, Nagisa?

00:22:09.100 --> 00:22:10.790
Let's go, Honoka!

00:22:22.350 --> 00:22:25.390
<i>Ah- Let's go!</i>

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:29.330
<i>Get you! L-O-V-E Love Love!</i>

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:30.060
<i>Get you!</i>

00:22:29.630 --> 00:22:32.660
<i>I can't do this! I'd rather be a</i>

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:35.700
<i>young lady than a fighter and</i>

00:22:35.700 --> 00:22:38.240
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:42.270
<i>And melt your body and soul into sweets</i>

00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:48.050
<i>like chocolate parfait or handsome men</i>

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:52.380
<i>I'm at the age to seriously 
fall head over heels in love</i>

00:22:52.380 --> 00:22:55.450
<i>I wanted to confess my love again today</i>

00:22:56.590 --> 00:22:59.960
<i>For the sake of the earth 
For the sake of everyone</i>

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:06.460
<i>That's good, too, but haven't 
you forgotten something?</i>

00:23:07.570 --> 00:23:14.070
<i>I'm a teenager with a heart 
throbbing exciting dream</i>

00:23:14.070 --> 00:23:20.580
<i>I don't want to lose that 
normal everyday routine</i>

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:23.310
<i>I just can't do this! 
It's romance rather than</i>

00:23:23.310 --> 00:23:26.550
<i>stress, isn't it?</i>

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:28.720
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode.</i>

00:23:28.720 --> 00:23:32.320
<i>Isn't that the best source of power?</i>

00:23:32.320 --> 00:23:35.530
<i>I just can't do this! I'd rather cuddle</i>

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:38.330
<i>than fight and...</i>

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:40.570
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:40.570 --> 00:23:43.230
<i>That's the most peaceful way</i>

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:49.810
<i>So why am I stuffing my face 
with chocolates like this?</i>

00:23:54.240 --> 00:23:55.510
What's wrong?

00:23:55.510 --> 00:23:57.290
Mepple's been taken away!

00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:58.730
What am I going to do? What shall I do?

00:23:58.730 --> 00:23:59.550
Calm down!

00:23:59.550 --> 00:24:01.280
He really seemed to be suffering.

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:02.670
He might be sick.

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:04.540
That's terrible! We'd 
better get him back fast.

00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:05.580
How can we do it?

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:07.410
Think, Nagisa!

00:24:08.990 --> 00:24:10.760
I can't think of anything mepo!

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:11.390
Mepo?

00:24:13.160 --> 00:24:15.400
"GIVE HIM BACK! 
THE GREAT MEPO MEPO STRATEGY"

00:24:15.380 --> 00:24:17.770
What are we going to do 
mepo? What shall we do mepo?

00:24:17.770 --> 00:24:20.260
Nagisa! What's with all the "mepos"?
